-- ==========================================================================
-- 0003_requirements.sql -- the cheat sheets as a requirement matrix.
--
-- 728 rows across 17 categories, derived from the category workbooks.
-- This is SEED DATA, not code, on purpose: when the cheat sheets are revised,
-- the change is a migration and a re-seed and no application logic moves.
--
-- kind = 'spec_field'  the answer belongs in a BWS spec column
-- kind = 'readiness'   the answer must be known but BWS has no column for it
--                      (TOE agreement, deposit, prototype, fabric quantities,
--                      pattern direction, lighting and power)
--
-- The prompts are the sheets' own wording, typos included, because that is
-- what the people using them will recognise. `section` groups them the way the
-- sheet does.
--
-- tgq_levels names the levels (simple / complex / hero) at which the question
-- must be answered before the item can be QUOTED. Every row starts at all
-- three, which is today's position: everything is required of everything. When
-- Matthew's TGQ workbook comes back the change is to these literals and
-- nothing else -- a tick in the workbook means "we can quote that level
-- without this", so applying it only ever REMOVES a level from a row. An empty
-- array is a question that never holds up a quote.
--
-- required_at_gate is deliberately NULL on every row. No cheat sheet mentions
-- TG0, TG1 or TG2 anywhere; assigning gates is an authoring job nobody has
-- done, and inventing one here would put words in its owner's mouth.
--
-- The mapping from a question to a BWS field is this seed's only judgement,
-- and it is the part to review first. A question with no confident field is
-- 'readiness' rather than a guess -- a wrong field id silently writes an
-- answer into the wrong BWS column at export.
--
-- Re-running updates in place, keyed on (category, sort_order). It never
-- deletes: answers reference requirements with `on delete restrict`, so a
-- requirement that disappears from a revised sheet must be retired
-- deliberately, with its answers dealt with, not dropped by a re-seed.
-- ==========================================================================

